#+TITLE: vpopmail — DSMR Package Documentation
#+AUTHOR: Brian O'Reilly <fade@deepsky.com>
#+DATE: 2026-03-22

* Summary

~vpopmail~ packages vpopmail 5.6.13 with a PostgreSQL authentication
backend.  It provides virtual domain and user management for qmail: the
~vadddomain~, ~vadduser~, and related tools create and manage email accounts
stored in the ~vpopmail~ PostgreSQL database.  ~vdelivermail~ delivers mail
into vpopmail Maildir directories.  ~vchkpw~ authenticates users for SMTP
submission (port 587).  Passwords are stored as SHA-512 crypt hashes.

The companion ~vpopmail-dev~ package installs headers and the ~lib_deps~ file
needed to build qmail with chkuser recipient verification.

| Field         | Value                               |
|---------------+-------------------------------------|
| Source        | vpopmail                            |
| Binaries      | vpopmail, vpopmail-dev              |
| Version       | 5.6.13-1                            |
| Architecture  | any                                 |
| Home          | ~/home/vpopmail/~                   |
| Domains       | ~/home/vpopmail/domains/~           |
| Config        | ~/home/vpopmail/etc/vpopmail.pgsql~ |
| Target        | Debian 13 Trixie                    |

* Description

vpopmail manages email accounts that are independent of Unix system
accounts.  Each virtual domain gets a directory under
~/home/vpopmail/domains/<domain>/~.  Each user gets a sub-directory
containing a Maildir and a ~.qmail~ file.  qmail delivers to these Maildirs
via ~vdelivermail~; SMTP submission authentication uses ~vchkpw~ (setuid root,
owned root:vchkpw).

** Why PostgreSQL instead of CDB?

vpopmail originally supported CDB, LDAP, MySQL, and others.  Starting with
dovecot 2.3.13 and fully in 2.4, dovecot removed its native vpopmail passdb
and checkpassword passdb drivers.  The only viable path for dovecot
authentication against vpopmail accounts is SQL.  This build therefore uses
~--enable-auth-module=pgsql~ so the vpopmail database can be queried directly
by dovecot's ~passdb sql~ driver.

** Password storage

~--enable-clear-passwd=n~ is set.  Passwords are stored as SHA-512 crypt
hashes (~$6$...~) in the ~pw_passwd~ column of the ~vpopmail~ table.  Clear
text is never stored.

** PostgreSQL database

The PostgreSQL role and database must exist before installing the package.
The postinst writes the credential file:

- Database: ~vpopmail~
- User: ~vpopmail~ with full rights on the ~vpopmail~ database
- Credentials written to ~/home/vpopmail/etc/vpopmail.pgsql~ (640, root:vchkpw)
- Format: ~host|port|user|password|database~

The vpopmail tools auto-create the schema tables (~vpopmail~, ~dir_control~,
etc.) on first ~vadddomain~ call.

* TL;DR Runtime Documentation

** Domain management

#+BEGIN_SRC sh
# Add a virtual domain
sudo /home/vpopmail/bin/vadddomain example.com postmaster-password

# Remove a virtual domain (destroys all mail and users)
sudo /home/vpopmail/bin/vdeldomain example.com

# List domains
sudo /home/vpopmail/bin/vdominfo
#+END_SRC

** User management

#+BEGIN_SRC sh
# Add a user
sudo /home/vpopmail/bin/vadduser user@example.com password

# Change password
sudo /home/vpopmail/bin/vpasswd user@example.com

# Delete a user
sudo /home/vpopmail/bin/vdeluser user@example.com

# Show user info
sudo /home/vpopmail/bin/vuserinfo user@example.com

# List users in a domain
sudo /home/vpopmail/bin/vdominfo -v example.com
#+END_SRC

** Filesystem layout

#+BEGIN_SRC
/home/vpopmail/
├── bin/            # vpopmail utilities (vadddomain, vadduser, vdelivermail, …)
├── domains/
│   └── example.com/
│       ├── .qmail-default     # "| /home/vpopmail/bin/vdelivermail '' delete"
│       ├── postmaster/
│       │   └── Maildir/
│       └── user/
│           ├── .qmail
│           └── Maildir/
│               ├── cur/
│               ├── new/       # ← qmail delivers here
│               └── tmp/
├── etc/
│   └── vpopmail.pgsql         # PostgreSQL credentials (640 root:vchkpw)
└── include/                   # Headers (vpopmail-dev)
#+END_SRC

** PostgreSQL credentials

#+BEGIN_SRC sh
# Read credentials (requires root or vchkpw group membership)
sudo cat /home/vpopmail/etc/vpopmail.pgsql
# Output: host|port|user|password|database
# Example: localhost|5432|vpopmail|<password>|vpopmail
#+END_SRC

** Manual PostgreSQL setup

#+BEGIN_SRC sh
PASS=$(openssl rand -base64 18 | tr -d '/+=')
sudo -u postgres psql <<SQL
CREATE DATABASE vpopmail;
CREATE USER vpopmail WITH PASSWORD '${PASS}';
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE vpopmail TO vpopmail;
\c vpopmail
GRANT ALL ON SCHEMA public TO vpopmail;
SQL
echo "localhost|5432|vpopmail|${PASS}|vpopmail" | \
  sudo tee /home/vpopmail/etc/vpopmail.pgsql
sudo chmod 640 /home/vpopmail/etc/vpopmail.pgsql
sudo chown root:vchkpw /home/vpopmail/etc/vpopmail.pgsql
#+END_SRC

** vchkpw authentication (SMTP submission)

~vchkpw~ is used by the ~qmail-submission~ supervise script to authenticate
users on port 587.  It reads a username and password from the authenticating
client, looks up the user in the vpopmail PostgreSQL database, verifies the
SHA-512 crypt hash, and execs the next program (typically qmail-smtpd) if
successful.

#+BEGIN_SRC sh
# Verify vchkpw is setuid root
ls -la /home/vpopmail/bin/vchkpw
# -rwsr-x--- 1 root vchkpw ...  /home/vpopmail/bin/vchkpw
#+END_SRC

** PostgreSQL schema tables

vpopmail creates its own tables on first ~vadddomain~.  The primary table:

#+BEGIN_SRC sql
-- Key columns of the vpopmail table
SELECT pw_name, pw_domain, pw_passwd, pw_dir
FROM vpopmail
WHERE pw_name = 'user' AND pw_domain = 'example.com';
#+END_SRC

** Quota management

#+BEGIN_SRC sh
# Set a 100 MB quota
sudo /home/vpopmail/bin/vsetuserquota user@example.com 102400S

# Show current quota usage
sudo /home/vpopmail/bin/vuserinfo -Q user@example.com
#+END_SRC

** Rebuilding from source

#+BEGIN_SRC sh
cd /path/to/dsmr-vpopmail
dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
#+END_SRC

Requires: ~debhelper-compat~, ~autoconf~, ~automake~, ~libtool~,
~libpq-dev~, and ~qmail-uids-gids~ pre-installed.
